WEBVTT

00:07:59.710 --> 00:08:01.806
he was a really, really bright kid,

00:08:01.830 --> 00:08:04.786
but not often in my classroom.

00:08:04.810 --> 00:08:09.886
And when we were talking
about what was coming next,

00:08:09.910 --> 00:08:11.716
I mean, I will really never forget.

00:08:11.740 --> 00:08:15.016
He said, "Miss, I'm going to be dead
by the time I'm 30.

00:08:15.040 --> 00:08:18.256
So, like, what does this matter?"

00:08:18.280 --> 00:08:20.277
AG: Conrey wanted to make a difference.

00:08:20.301 --> 00:08:22.586
She poured everything she had
into teaching.

00:08:22.610 --> 00:08:25.516
The workload was intense and exhausting.

00:08:25.540 --> 00:08:28.946
CC: My general workday
was typically around 12 hours.

00:08:28.970 --> 00:08:32.326
That didn't include any,
like, planning, or I don't know,